                <pb facs="0379" n="373" sameAs="frus:frus1894app2/pg373"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Wharton to Mr. Stevens.</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 59.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1892-10-26"><hi rendition="#italic">October 26,
                        1892</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have received your dispatch No. 70, of
                    the 8th instant, in relation to the political situation in Hawaii. It has been
                    read with much interest and attention.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">William F. Wharton</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Acting Secretary</hi>.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
